  "question": {
    "text": "A circular disc of mass <math><mtext>M</mtext></math> and radius <math><mtext>R</mtext></math> is rotating about its axis with angular speed <math><mrow><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math>. If another stationary disc having radius <math><mrow><mfrac><mtext>R</mtext><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></math> and same mass <math><mtext>M</mtext></math> is dropped co-axially on to the rotating disc. Gradually both discs attain constant angular speed <math><mrow><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>. The energy lost in the process is <math><mrow><mtext>p%</mtext></mrow></math> of the initial energy. Value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> is ______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9dcc6c60-7ca4-4e1a-894f-c1416b348768-image.png\" style=\"width: 351px; height: 128px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi></math></p><p>Final&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math>Percentage loss in kinetic energy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>loss</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>",
